<title>INDIA: India ACC 96/97 net plunges.</title>
<headline>India ACC 96/97 net plunges.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-06-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to March 31, 1997.</p>
<p>	     (in million rupees unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit		769.2    vs	2,267.8</p>
<p>    Sales		  24,692.2    vs     23,334.6</p>
<p>    Div/interest income   192.3    vs	  263.6</p>
<p>    Other income	    388.1    vs	  630.1</p>
<p>    Total income	 25,272.6    vs     24,228.3</p>
<p>    Div (in rupees)	  30.0    vs	   70.0</p>
<p>    Interest		1,182.9    vs	  980.9</p>
<p>    Gross profit	  1,682.7    vs	3,474.2</p>
<p>    Depreciation	    793.5    vs	  631.8</p>
<p>    Tax			 120.0    vs	  595.0</p>
<p>Note - Associated Cement Companies Ltd is India largest cement maker. In the previous year net profit was arrived at after accounting for extraordinary items 20.4 million rupees. In the latest year there was no such provisions.</p>
<p>The company did not give further details.</p>
<p>--Bombay newsroom +91-22-265-9000</p>
